  "_comment": "exposed_files and api_docs are the original sections (extended). Probe with GET (or HEAD then GET) and treat a hit as real only if the response is 200, is not a soft-404 (compare with a random-path baseline), and the body matches the file type (e.g. '[core]' for /.git/config, 'APP_KEY=' / 'DB_PASSWORD' for .env, 'SQL' dump markers for *.sql, 'swagger'/'openapi' for API docs). admin_panels, cloud_storage_probes and well_known_security are NEW optional sections: they are discovery lists (presence != vulnerability) and require scanner support. Everything is passive/read-only discovery.",
